          "explanation": "Douglass opens his 1845 Narrative by noting that enslaved people on the Eastern Shore had no more knowledge of their ages \"than horses know of theirs.\" This was deliberate. A person without a birthday has no identity rooted in time, no claim to history, no anchor for selfhood. Douglass treats this small omission as a window into slavery's larger project: the systematic erasure of personhood. He estimated 1817 in the Narrative; later research placed his birth in February 1818.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Why no birthday?</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"170\" width=\"900\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">DOUGLASS'S WORDS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"275\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"22\">\"I have no accurate knowledge of my age,</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"22\">never having seen any authentic record</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"22\">containing it.\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"378\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Narrative, Chapter 1</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"410\" width=\"900\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">DELIBERATE ERASURE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"As little as horses know of theirs\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"550\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Time-anchored identity withheld</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"585\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">A small omission, a systemic project</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"650\" width=\"900\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WHAT IT MEANT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">No birthday = no claim to history</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">No lineage = no selfhood in time</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"825\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Personhood erased at the root</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"900\" width=\"700\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Douglass estimated 1817</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"985\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Archives later confirmed February 1818</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1020\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">From Aaron Anthony's slave ledger</text></svg>",
            "caption": "A withheld birthday is a withheld self"
          }
